# Weather
// The weather in the city you pick:  now, big, then the next 12 hours.
// It comes from Open-Meteo, a server other people run:  Weather.api.spell, as `spell place ingest` wrote it.
// What each weather code looks like, in words and as an emoji, is in Sky.spell.

## The app:  a city to pick, and its forecast

weather is an app
	its "cities" is a list of cities
	its "place" is text
		// The city picked, by its name:  what the picker holds
	when creating it
		add a new city with name "Berlin", latitude = 52.52, longitude = 13.41 to its cities
		add a new city with name "New York", latitude = 40.71, longitude = -74.01 to its cities
		add a new city with name "Tokyo", latitude = 35.68, longitude = 139.69 to its cities
		add a new city with name "Buenos Aires", latitude = -34.6, longitude = -58.38 to its cities
		set its place to "Berlin"
	its "city" is the first city in its cities where its name is the place
	its "forecasts" is every forecast where its latitude is the latitude of the city and its longitude is the longitude of the city
		// The city's, from Open-Meteo:  asked for by where it is;  it answers with one

	to draw it
		<container text>
			<stack spacing="lg">
				<form value={it}>
					<select name="place" aria-label="City">
						<for city in its cities>
							<item value={its name}>{its name}</item>
						</for>
					</select>
				</form>
				<for its forecasts loading="Asking Open-Meteo" failed="Open-Meteo can't be reached just now." />
				<text size="small" color="grey">From <link link="https://open-meteo.com">Open-Meteo</link>, in your own units.</text>
			</stack>
		</container>

## A city:  where it is on Earth

a "city" is a thing
	its "name" is text
	its "latitude" is a number
	its "longitude" is a number

## A forecast:  the weather now, big, then the next 12 hours in a row

a forecast
	to draw it
		<stack spacing="lg">
			<segment padded="very">
				<stack align="center" spacing="xs">
					<emoji name={picture the weather (its current's weather code)} size="large" />
					<statistic size="huge">
						<value>{its current's temperature}</value>
					</statistic>
					<text size="large">{name the weather (its current's weather code)}</text>
				</stack>
			</segment>
			<segment>
				<stack direction="horizontal" spacing="lg" class="hours">
					{draw each hour in its hours}
				</stack>
			</segment>
		</stack>

## An hour:  its time, its weather and its temperature

an hour
	to draw it
		<stack align="center" spacing="xs">
			<text size="small" color="grey">{its time as a short time}</text>
			<emoji name={picture the weather (its weather code)} size="small" />
			<text>{its temperature}</text>
		</stack>
